<TITLE>Camshaft</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>High-strength alloy cast iron has been adopted for both the intake and exhaust camshafts, and the cam noses have been chill treated to ensure durability. Also, the cam lobes have been made narrower to reduce weight and friction loss. For lubrication of the cam journals, oil is supplied from the oil hole in the center of the camshaft.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The working angle of the intake camshaft has been increased for higher lift, and valve timing has been optimized to increase output.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
